A line may be bound twice.
The interrupt would reach whichever Irq the walk finds first
and the other would stay armed on a line it never hears;
at most one Irq is bound to any line.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test smp-test qemu-replay
Report: irq is missing from the line table

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -558,7 +558,7 @@ static int op_irq_line(struct thread *t, uint32_t slot, const struct cap *cap,
             return err;
         }
         /* The cores' line is bound already, to the kernel. */
-        if (line_binding(first) != NULL || line_is_cores(first)) {
+        if (line_is_cores(first)) {
             return KERR_OVERLAP;
         }
         /* The invoked slot is cleared below, so it may receive the Irq capability. */
